# Model checkpoints

- Saved model checkpoints can be found in the src/polarbert/checkpoints folder, and typically have a `.pth` (plain PyTorch) or `.ckpt` (Pytorch-Lightning) extension.
- NEVER DELETE ANY CHECKPOINTS. Instead, ask the user to do it manually if needed.
- Checkpoints in the src/polarbert/checkpoints/results subfolder are experiment results, and are particularly important.
- When performing a new experiment, always choose a unique and descriptive name for its checkpoints, without any spaces.
- Checkpoints are large binary files. Do not attempt to read them into your own context.
